Reason:
The `nouveau_conn_mode_clock_valid()` function incorrectly handled the validation of clock values for display modes, particularly for 3D frame packing. The logic that doubled the clock value for 3D frame packing was flawed and led to potential miscalculations of the clock frequency, resulting in invalid mode statuses being returned.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if ((mode->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_MASK) == DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING)
	clock *= 2;

if (clock < min_clock)
	return MODE_CLOCK_LOW;
if (clock > max_clock)
	return MODE_CLOCK_HIGH;
```
Reason:
The logic for handling 3D frame packing has been moved directly into the `nouveau_connector_mode_valid()` function, eliminating the need for the separate `nouveau_conn_mode_clock_valid()` function. This change improves clarity and correctness by ensuring that the clock validation logic is integrated into the main mode validation process, thus preventing the previous miscalculations and ensuring valid mode statuses are returned.

